{:edb/db-before-t 2552 :edb/db-after-t 2553 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535865 50 #inst "2026-10-09T09:22:04.757Z" 13194139535865 true] [17592186229108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371160 13194139535865 true] [17592186229108 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371167 13194139535865 true] [17592186229109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371174 13194139535865 true] [17592186229109 1020 #edb/ref 17592186371178 13194139535865 true] [17592186229610 1017 #edb/ref 17592186228095 13194139535865 false] [17592186229610 1017 #edb/ref 17592186371154 13194139535865 true] [17592186229610 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535865 true] [17592186229610 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x{y}^{2},\\,y(1)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx=1,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ used in the first step?" 13194139535865 true] [17592186229610 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$y^{′} = 2xy^{2}, y(1) = 1$\nUsing the trapezoidal method with step size $Δx = 1$, the new value $y_{new}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g(y_{new}) = 0$ at each step. Which of the following is the **specific function** $g(y_{new})$ used in the first step?" 13194139535865 false] [17592186229610 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nIn this example, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x{y}^{2}+2{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+x{y}^{2}+{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand moving all terms to the left-hand side gives the equation\n\n$$\n{y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-x{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, the general form of the function $g$ for step size $Δx=1$ is\n\n$$\ng({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-{x}_{\\text{new}}({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-y-x{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first step, the new $x$ value is\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function used in the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g({y}_{\\text{new}}) & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1-1(1)^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371155 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371156 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371157 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371158 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1000 #edb/ref 17592186371159 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1041 "selection" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1104 #edb/ref 17592186371156 13194139535865 true] [17592186371154 1110 #uuid "b5cc6747-a74a-5506-9d19-89bac4895967" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371155 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-1" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535865 true] [17592186371155 1111 #uuid "0f195b54-0ce6-5a05-8e50-a1f62e3633f0" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371156 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new}}-2({y}_{\\text{new}})^{2}-2" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535865 true] [17592186371156 1111 #uuid "160e84c4-5c45-5dbf-804a-cb8c45fce94a" 13194139535865 true] [17592186371157 1034 "g({y}_{\\text{new}})={y}_{\\text{new